{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1128359-animal-stats-different-with-editions","id":1128359,"title":"Animal Stats different with Editions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-13T00:55:56-07:00","id":1128359,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Animal Stats different with Editions","content":"So curious, what method of Animal stats do people use? I use revised Sensibilities, but I am open to change, as in you give them stats roughly based on what they could do if they were human, so bears are often strength 7, but a smaller black bear could be strength 6 and a gigantic strong male grizzly or polar bear could be strength 8. Earlier editions and some books may have really wonky stats. And Darkages post Revised used animal stats closer to the Exalted 3rd ed paradigm, where there stats aren't really human stats, just stats based off of their story weight, so a Horse may have strength 3 or 4, even though that means mean can be stronger then them, you just hand wave it.<br /> <br /> Like what about an Elephant? 9 or 10 in say strength were often their used stats, what would you use?<br /> <br /> I often used Shifter animal traits as good basis, with the understanding that often their animal form was idealized for their mythic duties and legends, so Lupus form is stronger and faster then homid, and becoming a rat doesn't cripple your stats too bad.<br /> <br /> How do you all do it? The impression I got was a lot of people just used the simple method of using whatever stat their core used, so animals are different depending if they are doing whatever edition. As a storyteller I am never fond of doing whats in the book if there are more attractive alternatives, like I use revised multiple action rules, unless they use celerity or rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T05:36:28-07:00","id":1128401,"title":"","content":"I generally use my own statistics because the given statistics are quite strange. For example, Elephants can drag an average of 5 tons (9 tons is the record), which would make them around 50 times as strong as the average human. If you assume that you can drag twice what you can carry, that would give elephants an effective Strength 14, which makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T06:25:40-07:00","id":1128415,"title":"","content":"I use the Bygone Bestiary for most rules pertaining to animals. It was a one shot source book on mythical and mundane animals for use in multiples splats. It introduces Bears with strength 5-7 as base stats so going above 5 is accepted.<br /> <br /> One thing you have to keep in mind is that their strength rating is used mostly for figuring out how much damage they do in combat. The average weight most sources say an elephant can lift 650 lbs unassisted under strength 5 but with help (example given was they tied a leather cord around logs for the elephant to bite) they were able to lift up to 1100 lbs, but that is only talking about the strength of its trunk alone as the most muscular parts of an elephant are incapable of lifting. So in the case of an elephant I would have different strength ratings depending on what it is trying to do because like Aya mentioned, I would allow them to drag or carry weights much higher then what their trunks can lift alone.<br /> <br /> They would also have a Trample attack which would add dice to their already high strength but it still wouldn't do their full strength damage because the animal never uses its full strength, it just uses its body mass. And I would give them a Stomp attack they did more damage then that because they would be using more of their actual strength in that attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T07:08:39-07:00","id":1128432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1128359-animal-stats-different-with-editions?p=1128415#post1128415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use the Bygone Bestiary for most rules pertaining to animals. It was a one shot source book on mythical and mundane animals for use in multiples splats. It introduces Bears with strength 5-7 as base stats so going above 5 is accepted.<br /> <br /> One thing you have to keep in mind is that their strength rating is used mostly for figuring out how much damage they do in combat. The average weight most sources say an elephant can lift 650 lbs unassisted under strength 5 but with help (example given was they tied a leather cord around logs for the elephant to bite) they were able to lift up to 1100 lbs, but that is only talking about the strength of its trunk alone as the most muscular parts of an elephant are incapable of lifting. So in the case of an elephant I would have different strength ratings depending on what it is trying to do because like Aya mentioned, I would allow them to drag or carry weights much higher then what their trunks can lift alone.<br /> <br /> They would also have a Trample attack which would add dice to their already high strength but it still wouldn't do their full strength damage because the animal never uses its full strength, it just uses its body mass. And I would give them a Stomp attack they did more damage then that because they would be using more of their actual strength in that attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot about the dangers of being gored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T14:14:08-07:00","id":1128572,"title":"","content":"Or eaten (yes, elephants occasionally swallow humans whole when sufficiently irritated).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T10:38:27-07:00","id":1130345,"title":"","content":"Ok, you win, folks. <i>I finally think elephants are cool.</i> I'm sitting here regretting many past statements. I'm so sorry, elephants. I should have trusted Hannibal. You were always worthy of my admiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T08:18:10-07:00","id":1130828,"title":"","content":"I use M20, since that's the game I'm running. I don't usually think about their stats too much tbh. It's not really all that important to the narrative. Stats only come up in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}